FR-1 Asset Registration (FR-1.1 to FR-1.14)
- How an Asset Custodian registers an asset and publishes it.
- Required fields: name, description, category, quantity, owner,
  department, location, condition.
- Optional fields: subcategory, specs, brand/model, serial number,
  purchase date, estimated value (AED), material type.
- Rules for invalid input, photos (max 5) and documents (max 3),
  unique asset IDs, duplicate serial warnings, drafts, audit log.
- Registration must still work if the AI is down.
 
FR-3 Requests and Reservations (FR-3.1 to FR-3.14)
- How a Requester asks for a listed asset or for a general need.
- Request fields: department, category, purpose, quantity,
  required date, delivery location (+ optional specs, condition, urgency).
- The requested quantity is held so the same item is not given
  to two departments.
- Requests can be edited while Submitted and cancelled before handover.
- Holds expire after 10 working days.
 
FR-4 Approvals and Transfers (FR-4.1 to FR-4.16)
- Four steps: release (owner) -> approval (Administrator)
  -> transfer (collection or delivery) -> receipt (receiving department).
- High-value items need a second approval from the Procurement Officer.
- AI never approves or transfers anything; a person always decides.
- Custody and location only change when receipt is confirmed.
- Disputes (damaged / wrong item) go to the Administrator.
 
